course: dictionary
lesson: 7846
title: Radiation: energy that travels
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Radiation is energy that travels through space as invisible waves or tiny particles. Light, heat and X-rays are all kinds of radiation. The Sun warms the Earth by radiation, so you feel its warmth even though you cannot see it travelling.
explain: Radiation can be harmless or dangerous, so the words around it give you clues. «In 1986 a reactor at the Chornobyl power plant in Ukraine exploded and spread radiation, and people had to leave a large area around it.» People leaving their homes tells you this radiation is dangerous.
explain: Radiation can also help people. Doctors use strong rays as a treatment for some cancers. Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence? «The Sun warms the Earth by ___» Radiation fits, so you know you have understood it.
fact: Radiation is energy that travels as invisible waves or tiny particles.
fact: Light, heat, X-rays and radio waves are all types of radiation.
fact: «Radiation» often means the dangerous kind given off by radioactive things, which can harm living things in large amounts.
fact: Radiation is used as a medical treatment for some cancers, using strong rays.
fact: UV radiation from the Sun can cause sunburn, which is why we wear sun cream.
exercise: «The pine trees nearest the reactor were killed by radiation and turned red-brown.» What killed the trees? | Ducks | Wind | Snow | *Radiation
exercise: Which of these is a kind of radiation, energy that travels as waves? | A cloud | *Light | A rock | A spoon
exercise: Why did people have to leave the area around the Chornobyl reactor? | To go on holiday | Because it was raining | *Because radiation from the exploded reactor had spread over the area | To visit the power plant
test: Which of these is a medical use of radiation? | *Treating some cancers with strong rays | Cleaning floors | Making paper | Growing tomatoes
test: Why do we wear sun cream in summer? | To change our hair colour | To make our skin shine | To keep bugs away from our hair | *To protect our skin from UV radiation that causes sunburn
exam: Which sentence uses radiation in the dangerous sense? | «Light travels from the Sun to the Earth.» | «The Sun warms the Earth by radiation.» | *«The pine trees nearest the reactor were killed by radiation.» | «Radio waves carry music to your house.»
